   "job_title": "C# .NET Developer (Intermediate) - Entry Level",
   "description": "You'll build and ship features that real users touch every day, for a bank's digital channels team in Randburg. It's a practical job: you'll see what you got done before you go home. \n\n You'll be based at a bank's digital channels team in Randburg. Living nearby, or on a taxi route to it, really helps. Start date: as soon as possible for the right person. \n\n What your day looks like  Join daily stand-ups and sprint planning  Pair with junior developers to unblock them  Build and consume REST or GraphQL APIs  Write, test and refactor code in your team's main language  Review teammates' pull requests with useful comments  Must-haves  You can explain technical choices to non-technical people  Good SQL and understanding of relational databases  Experience writing automated tests  Solid Git habits: branches, pull requests and meaningful commit messages  A computer science or IT qualification, or a portfolio that proves you can build  What you get  Hybrid or fully remote work  Laptop and data allowance  Paid certification exams and learning budget  Medical aid and retirement fund  Applying, step by step  Make sure the role, the hours and working in Randburg really suit you before you apply.  Get these ready, because shortlisted people are asked for them straight away: degree or diploma certificate, list of projects with the tech stack you used on each plus link to your GitHub, GitLab or portfolio.  Send your details with the form below. Add one or two lines about similar work you've done.  Keep your phone on. Shortlisted applicants are contacted by call, SMS or WhatsApp within 10 working days.  Your application joins the How2Apply talent pool for this role, and we put shortlisted people forward to employers hiring in and around Randburg. \n\n Applying is free. Nobody from How2Apply will ever ask you to pay for anything to get this job. \n\n Tips to get shortlisted  Start your CV with your stack in one line, such as \"C#, .NET 8, SQL Server, Azure\", then your years on it.  For each job, name one thing you built and its impact, like \"cut checkout load time by 40%\".",
